        "id": 1265562
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-21T23:09:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we have any experience of failures like flash write failures etc from test devices etc? If so, we might be able to simply retry writing an object and invalidate the previous attempt with a retry limit. We also might need a way of ignoring a page if the page header cannot be written as intended.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 244,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 244,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "c8b9c9101a9cf93016ea83e99b80832737749357",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "918133f4_8bb2019b",
        "filename": "common/new_nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 244,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-22T18:40:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we have not seen instances of catastrophic flash failures yet, and this patchset is meant to make flash failures due to wear much less likely on top of that. We might want to think about working around persistent flash failures, but it should be a separate enhancement.",
      "parentUuid": "9e4e110a_5fbb9f09",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 244,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 244,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "c8b9c9101a9cf93016ea83e99b80832737749357",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "40397812_1969ecba",
        "filename": "common/new_nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 400,
      "author": {
        "id": 1265562
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-21T23:09:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is some potential for pointer alignment issues here. It isn\u0027t a problem if data_offset is only ever set/changed in a safe way.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 400,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 400,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "c8b9c9101a9cf93016ea83e99b80832737749357",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2c7423df_01c2c842",
        "filename": "common/new_nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 400,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-22T18:40:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this is a good point: there are issues with unaligned access, but they are addressed in the code using the pointer - when this function is called we don\u0027t know what the intended use is.\n\nAnd since page header address is guaranteed to be aligned properly, the user of this function has full control on the alignment of the result.",
      "parentUuid": "40397812_1969ecba",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 400,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 400,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "c8b9c9101a9cf93016ea83e99b80832737749357",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
