      "writtenOn": "2019-03-21T23:09:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it be preferable to save the container regardless of type (excluding deleted containers and delimiters) assuming certain fields like the size are always present? Alternatively you could reserve a group of types for ones that should be copied and ones that should not.\n\nI bring this up because we might want to be able to support rolling back without data loss.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 802,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 803,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "c8b9c9101a9cf93016ea83e99b80832737749357",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "631a01a9_6591c16a",
        "filename": "common/new_nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 803,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-22T18:40:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this scheme allows for introducing new object types, especially since the (key,value) pair is so flexible, so I would not worry about rollback in this case.",
      "parentUuid": "a9193584_bf6c784f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 802,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 803,
        "endChar": 9
      },
